<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela is alleged to have assisted a deadly drone strike that killed two soldiers in Colombia's Choco department, while a separate bomb attack near a military base killed four civilians, including an infant. President De la Espriella has renewed a military offensive against dissident groups and ordered additional bombings and aerial spraying following the Planadas bombing. The United Nations has renewed its mission in Colombia but excluded rural reform, and the government launched a broader offensive after seven attacks in six days. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxPb2p4akFMdUxTeWtlSkhaLXZBdXdyWkZLSFlPMm1EbDhGelRsUVlxV0N3cnYwZlZZemZiQWRrdTM0RVhhTG5PbDVVcy0xaVNEVW56d2FEYnA0ZGs2aEpnSFlmV2FuV3NHZ1F3N1pENC1Xa2JGeWJ3emo4eGY3ZkdHODEzcFMyUWYyRU9LQ1NjM1J1d29LaEpDMG9Tdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE5fWW05WWFRdXd6bFJjVU5RMko0dHdmalg4RWJQeF9HRnRyd1VPS2VrWWF0T0haQ2l2WGppRU5EVE1xZU1PbE1VeFVMWFVVdmhJMXVhQVlvdFV6OHpv?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPaFg3czJSZGVsNUNiMEozTFEtRWQyX0hxaG12QjJ3b0E3U09SNGl5VXV6WG9OVTdpSExzX1QwNl93QktIMVhpNWNuTFVXNm9qZ1lBNk5EdnlXU0pPdjZnU1JPUzlaaFBTV3RoTE11b1pLUERYR2wyZURoWkV0bWd2QnFGd1Y5b3RfSHIxX1hkb2VxeXBPSTQzTEhnWV9sQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Orinoco Tribune&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxOZFg1c3NYNXNUU0VTblZfUFU2VG4tYVhicW1nYTkyaGpvRmlBMi13RjJKc0pnaEI2bGdiVF9lNDF2VGdpTDk2NU9GNEViT19iWXp0UkRTUC1BLXIxOVlNWmlNa0dKTTFoa0JZU1c0c2V2dXVfdjlXSE1rQVM2VkRhdlUyODBTVjZFUkRTUHdqRQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Balkanweb.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxOY09JM2NIVXRJbHVIN2